isorder, a condition characterized by pronounced changes in mood and energy levels. \"The list of bipolar musicians includes Scott Wyland, Pete Wenz, of Fallout Boy, Brian Wilson of the Beach Boys, Shenato Conor.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Sinead O'Connor","from_id":260915823316947,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Musicians With Disabilities","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=trMzjWWmbZo"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Bipolar Disorder","body":"A significant factor in Scott Weiland's and Mary Forsberg's struggles was their undiagnosed bipolar disorder, which led to extreme mood swings and poor judgment, often exacerbated by self-medication with drugs like crack. Doctors initially misdiagnosed him with severe depression, and the treatments did not control his manic episodes. \"A big part of their problems coping with life is that they were both undiagnosed sufferers of bipolar disorder, and this is a really important part of our story.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Scott Weiland","from_id":900011635688,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Scott Weiland: Part 3","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WfTq9d2YadY"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Bipolar Disorder","body":"Matthew Good is mentioned as a musician who suffers from bipolar disorder. \"Lou Reed, Axel Rose, Shenandoah Conner, Scott Wyland, rapper Chris Brown, Matthew Good, Adam Ant, Brittany Spears, Jack Irons, former drummer with the Chili Peppers, Scott Stap of Creed, Pete Wentz of Fallout Boy, Frank Sinatra.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Matthew Good","from_id":225588717211815,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Health Issues of Musicians","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NQgn0_mUh74"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Bipolar Disorder","body":"Adam Ant is listed among musicians identified as bipolar. \"Lou Reed, Axel Rose, Shenandoah Conner, Scott Wyland, rap